# Nothing here touches a home directory, a token or a secret. The messages
# say what each user does by hand.

post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
Run once per user, from a login session on Omarchy:
    acd-inbox install
It writes ~/.config/systemd/user/acd-inbox.service, copies the binary to
~/.local/bin and the plugin to ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/tonibergholm.agentcaller,
and offers a keybinding. Check it with: acd-inbox status
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'
acd-inbox install keeps its own copy of the binary in ~/.local/bin and its
own plugin files. After an upgrade each user runs `acd-inbox install` again
to refresh them, then restarts the shell: omarchy-restart-shell.
Settings and pairing secrets are not touched.
MSG
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'
Per-user copies are left in place. To remove them run `acd-inbox uninstall`
(the copy in ~/.local/bin works). Settings in ~/.config/acd-inbox and pairing
secrets in the keyring are never deleted by the package.
MSG
}
